Secrets are logical containers made up of zero or more immutable versions, that contain sensitive data.

USAGE:
  scw secret secret <command>

AVAILABLE COMMANDS:
  add-owner   Allow a product to use the secret
  cockpit     Open the Cockpit Grafana dashboard for this secret
  create      Create a secret
  delete      Delete a secret
  get         Get metadata using the secret's ID
  list        List secrets
  protect     Enable secret protection
  unprotect   Disable secret protection
  update      Update metadata of a secret

FLAGS:
  -h, --help[=true|false]                help for secret
      --list-sub-commands[=true|false]   List all subcommands

GLOBAL FLAGS:
  -B, --beta[=true|false]         Enable beta mode
  -c, --config string             The path to the config file
  -D, --debug[=true|false]        Enable debug mode
  -H, --no-headers[=true|false]   Skip headers in human output
  -o, --output string             Output format: json or human, see 'scw help output' for more info (default "human")
  -p, --profile string            The config profile to use

Use "scw secret secret [command] --help" for more information about a command.
